PATCH 533: FUN_0000_c86e -- the cockpit render method for object classes 7..14 was MISSING entirely.

Found by following TRAIN4's SIGSEGV after patch 531 moved it.  The fault was inside FUN_0000_f8e9 --
which is not a function entry at all but a loop head in an interrupt-disabled list-splice routine
(the real entry is 0xf909: `or bx,bx; pushf; cli; push ds; mov es,ds; mov ds,bx`) -- reached straight
from c4df's object-render dispatch.  A render method cannot be that, so the method vector was resolving
to nothing.

Measured at the fault: `g_fist_render_si = 0xb0ad`, `classid = word[DGROUP:0xb0ad] = 13`, `d549 = 0x1e`
(cockpit), `STRSEG = 0x2d74`.  c4df computes `mvec = word[STRSEG : classid*2 + 0x3632]`, and reading
that table out of a memory dump gives:

    classid  0..3 -> 0xc7ca      classid 4      -> 0xc5e7
    classid  5..6 -> 0xc829      classid 7..14  -> 0xc86e
    classid 15    -> 0xc5e7      classid 16     -> 0xc715      classid 17..19 -> 0xc5e7

So classid 13's method is 0xc86e.  Of those five targets, THREE are absent from the port -- 0xc715,
0xc829 and 0xc86e are neither defined nor present in the fist_icall fmap -- and between them they cover
classes 5..14 and 16, i.e. the bulk of the object registry.  Ghidra simply never promoted them.

This is the "un-seeded function" class, but reached through a DATA-DRIVEN method table rather than a
trap, which is why a trap-trace sweep (board:0001) did not turn it up.

0xc86e is three instructions:

    c86e: b4 0d        mov ah,0xd
    c870: e8 3f 00     call 0xc8b2
    c873: c3           ret

and is instruction-for-instruction the twin of FUN_0000_c70d (asm `c70d: mov ah,0xf; call c8b2; ret`),
which patch 463 already reconstructed for class 0x15:

    si = g_fist_render_si;
    FUN_0000_c8b2(CONCAT11(0xf,0), (classid*2), 0, si, 0);   /* bx=classid*2 live from c4df; bp -> 0 */

So this patch is that reconstruction verbatim with AH=0x0d, plus the declaration and the fist_icall
fmap entry so the dispatch can actually reach it.

Still missing and left on the board: 0xc829 (`call 0xc894; ret` -- and 0xc894 is ALSO absent) and
0xc715 (longer; reads byte[si+0x1c], indexes word[bx-0x17f3], calls 0xc8c2).

--- a/fist.c
+++ b/fist.c
